5. What is a Linux Distribution?
This is another important interview question.

Linux kernel alone is not a complete user-friendly operating system environment.

A Linux distribution combines the Linux kernel with system utilities, package management, libraries and applications.

Examples:










Ubuntu

Beginner friendly; commonly used on servers and desktops.











Red Hat Enterprise Linux

Enterprise Linux distribution.











Debian

Stable community distribution.











CentOS Stream

Enterprise Linux development stream.


