6. Practical Implementation – Ubuntu
Now it's your turn.

Open your Ubuntu terminal.

Execute these commands one by one.

Command 1 – Check Linux kernel information
uname -a


Purpose: Displays kernel and system information.

Command 2 – Check your hostname
hostnamectl


Purpose: Displays computer identification and operating system information.

Command 3 – Check current user
whoami


Purpose: Shows which user is currently logged in.

Command 4 – Check user and group IDs
id


Purpose: Displays your user ID (UID) and group IDs (GIDs).

Command 5 – Check system uptime
uptime


Purpose: Shows how long your computer has been running and system load averages.

Command 6 – Check Ubuntu version
cat /etc/os-release


Purpose: Displays operating system details.

You can also try:
lsb_release -a


